#  sha256 of every file in the gitsfa folder the builder makes (hashes only, no game data). b122: rebuilt from the
#  first complete Windows run (build 122 package, the reference install), after it was checked file by file: 465 files are
#  byte-identical to the data the port is tested with on the Vita (copy-to-vita); the 5 text files differed only by Windows
#  line ends ('\r\n', fixed: python\sitecustomize.py writes '\n'); the 13 radar <map>.gmm use the Lanczos radar step (the
#  Vita data: the dev path); the rest are listed below with how they are checked when their hash differs.
#  Video files whose bytes can vary with the PC (x264 / swscale take other code paths on CPUs without SSSE3; OpenCV's
#  inpainting, used for tut_v6, rounds differently in its Windows build): checked by decoding them (size, frame count).
#    ~ <name> video <width>x<height> <frames>
#  The light first-person meshes (b60): read and compared with the reference's mesh count and index total (within 5 %).
#    ~ <name> gfp <meshes> <indices>
#  Files of computed numbers (b122): light samples (.glgt), colour grading fits (.glut), skies (.gsky), the animation banks
#  (.gab: quantised quaternions; Linux and Windows differ in about 1 in 2000 values by one step), effect tables (.gfx),
#  navigation edges (.gnav), radar pictures (.gmm) and the Think Tank HUD portraits: the C library and numpy round the last
#  bit differently on other systems and CPUs; checked to be the same kind of file and exactly the reference's size.
#    ~ <name> size <first 4 bytes, hex> <bytes>
